## `isAnchorDoc` in `BusinessDocumentFinder`

**File:** `src/main/java/io/exoreaction/synthesis/report/BusinessDocumentFinder.java:142`

### Purpose

**Anchor documents are always included in report context regardless of their age.** When `synthesis report` filters business documents to a time period (e.g. `1w`, `2w`), the cutoff filter would normally exclude older files. Anchor docs bypass that cutoff — they're always passed to the AI as context because they represent persistent, authoritative state (not time-bounded activity).

The two anchor patterns are:
- `PIPELINE-STATUS` / `PIPELINE_STATUS` — the live pipeline status document
- `ACTIVITY-LOG` / `ACTIVITY_LOG` — the running activity log

### Implementation

```java
// :137 — the allowlist of name fragments
private static final List<String> ANCHOR_DOC_PATTERNS = List.of(
    "PIPELINE-STATUS", "PIPELINE_STATUS",
    "ACTIVITY-LOG", "ACTIVITY_LOG"
);

// :142 — detection logic: case-insensitive substring match
private static boolean isAnchorDoc(String fileName) {
    String upper = fileName.toUpperCase();
    return ANCHOR_DOC_PATTERNS.stream().anyMatch(upper::contains);
}

// :163 — used as a filter bypass in discover(workspaceRoot, topic, period)
return allDocs.stream()
    .filter(doc -> isAnchorDoc(doc.path().getFileName().toString())
            || doc.lastModified().isAfter(cutoff))
    .collect(Collectors.toList());
```

### Logic Summary

- Detection: uppercase the filename, check if any anchor pattern appears as a substring (so `MY-PIPELINE-STATUS.md` also matches)
- Effect: the `|| doc.lastModified().isAfter(cutoff)` short-circuits — anchor docs always pass the filter even if they haven't been touched within the report period
- Rationale: the AI report engine needs the full current state of the pipeline and activity log as context even if they were last updated outside the report window

Tracked under GitHub issue [#46](https://github.com/exoreaction/Synthesis/issues/46).

